  "scope": [
    "Versioned supplied-PCM narration cue contract, generated schema and public compiler. All three candidate families reuse relative cue references and original rig/relationship validators.",
    "Compile native picture/control/camera, live anchor annotation/leader, caption, supplied effect and unchanged narration tracks through one cue map. Recompile a shorter take without a nine-shot duration.",
    "Reject source/cue/motion/sample bounds, overlapping cues, conflicting writers, insufficient source and visible reading/action windows, invalid state order, camera hold/clip-plane changes, conflicting assets and sound tails. Hash track identities separately to keep IDs bounded.",
    "Expose deterministic first-output-frame-at-or-after-cue timing and integer PCM onset delay; retain original narration source sample count/hash and compare actual decoded sources/repeated video and audio.",
    "Dark caption/annotation backings repair the sampled contrast failure. Float32 spring driver-key precision repairs cross-runtime identity while preserving sampled geometry and exact GPU-byte checks."
  ],
  "qualification": "The live fixtures use synthetic local PCM, not spoken production narration. They verify compiler/timing/export behavior, all final native observations and independent bounded replay; no pilot or human listening/visual acceptance is inferred. Source cues retain exact PCM facts; visual/effect/motion placement follows the documented integer frame quantization with reported onset delay. The final frame quantum is distinct from source duration. Full label layout/readability, genuine spoken cue semantics, supported pack promotion, registry/coverage/typography, semantic report/other producer/whole-resource/lifetime accounting, remaining MS2 full gates and final installed refresh remain open.",
